    "issue": "oxyc/den-atlas#92",
    "what": "Corpus-visible acceptance for curated franchise rows and More Like This exclusion. The keys and era controls come from den-dataset's hand-checked franchise golden set. The issue's Van Veeteren control is not a case: none of its films is in the corpus, so no store can pass or fail it.",
    "rule": "A franchise is one continuity or rights line, with eras (Spider-Man's reboots, Beck's recasts, Eon's Bond). A separate production of the same source (the British Wallander, the non-Eon Bond films, a Sherlock Holmes adaptation) is not an era of it; it is apart, and reached through the title's Other versions row (owner's decision on #92, 2026-09-28; #112).",
    "scope": "Run `den-atlas franchise-check <dataset dir>` on the staged rebuilt store before deployment. This makes no network or model calls.",
    "ordering": "The seed era leads its route and every era retains release order, so each era below lists its titles in release order: the year, then Wikidata's finer date where it gives one. Beck's exact 46-title corpus group is pinned because the completed derive explicitly recorded that result.",
